WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.500
Tali: Moshe, I love you. May your life
and legacy and energy continue to live on.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:12.400
And I'm always thinking of you
in my heart. Love you.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.400
Shlomi: Moshe, I miss you. I know you're
looking at all of us from over there.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.500
Rest in peace.

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.700
Galia: Love you, Dod Moshe.

6
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.100
Keep doing where you are, what you have meant,
what you managed to do here on earth.

7
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:35.900
Ruthie (in Hebrew): My dear uncle,
I will never forget you.

8
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.100
Thank you for what you were in my life.
And may you rest in peace forever and ever.

9
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:52.100
Steve: Alav hashalom.
Peace be upon him.

10
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:59.500
Debbie: Moshe, you are a special gift
and truly exceptional. You will be missed.

11
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.700
Micah: I was just saying
thank you to Dod Moshe.

12
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.900
David Norsoph: Well, Moshe, keep smiling, and may the pool
of women be even more plentiful in heaven than on earth.

13
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.200
Spoiler alert. That's not really
how it works, okay?

14
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.900
You never know.

15
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.100
Mor: [a blessing, spoken quietly]

16
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.100
Aimee: Uncle Moshe, you will
live in our hearts forever.

17
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.900
David Gudai: Yitgadal v'yitkadash.

18
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.300
Daniel: Well, the only appropriate thing
for me is just to sing, really.

19
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.400
[Singing] Moshe-le,
I love you so much, Mo.

20
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.500
Love you. Miss you. Thank you for
having an amazing impact on my life.

21
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:51.400
And I will continue to share your spirit
and your happiness with the world. Thank you, Moshe.

22
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.700
Michael: L'ilui nishmat Moshe ben Sivia.

23
00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:01.400
[Blessing in Hebrew]
Amen.

24
00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:07.000
Jeremy: Moshe, may your memory and legacy continue
throughout all of us and all generations to come.

25
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:14.400
Jonathan: We will continue to honor Moshe
for as long as we live, and to remember him.

26
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.800
And he is going to continue to be
with us for as long as we live.

27
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.600
To Moshe Yeffet. We love you.

28
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:39.200
[Michael recites El Malei Rachamim
for Moshe ben Sivia]

29
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.200
Amen.
